### Page 1 of 5

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

City of Cheyenne Governing Body
FROM:

Robin Lockman, City Treasurer
DATE:

November 7, 2022
SUBJECT:
Annual Write-Off Per Resolution 4970

On November 14, 2022, the Governing Body will be referring a resolution to the Finance
Committee to write off $24,279 in uncollectible accounts of the City and $42,887 for the Board of
Public Utilities sanitation billings.  Per Resolution 4970, debts owed to the City that are at least
four years old, the customer is deceased or their debt has been discharged in bankruptcy are
considered “uncollectible”.
The type of debt under consideration for write off is as follows:

Please note that approval of this resolution does not prevent further collection efforts on the
accounts listed.  The collection agency will keep working on collecting these debts until the statute
of limitations ends, even if the accounts are removed from our financial records.  However, it is a
requirement under generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP) to write off a bad debt when
the related customer invoice is considered to be uncollectible.  Otherwise, the City will carry an
inordinately high accounts receivable balance that overstates the amount of outstanding customer
invoices that will eventually be converted into cash.
As always, if you have any questions on the policies and procedures in place, please give me a call
at 637-6336 or email at rlockman@cheyennecity.org.

Category
Amount
